  Definition of Loops

A loop is used to repeat a block of code multiple times until a condition is satisfied.

Instead of writing code again and again, we use loops.

Types of Loops in Python
for loop
while loop


for loop








numbers = [10, 15, 20, 25, 30]

total = 0
even = 0
odd = 0

for n in numbers:
    total += n
    
    if n % 2 == 0:
        even += 1
    else:
        odd += 1

print("Total:", total)
print("Even count:", even)
print("Odd count:", odd)


  while loop







total = 0
count = 0

while True:
    mark = int(input("Enter mark (-1 to stop): "))
    
    if mark == -1:
        break
    
    total += mark
    count += 1

if count > 0:
    avg = total / count
    print("Average:", avg)
else:
    print("No data entered")
